  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>When unpolarized light passes from Polaroid, then it becomes polarised light and intensity becomes half of the original, therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/912cf425-df11-4e8f-b3d6-290a6a77f598-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 79px;\" /></p><p>Given here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.</p><p>Using law of&nbsp;Malus&nbsp;for the second polariser,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p>We have, intensity of emergent light,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p></blockquote>",
